{
  "_comment": [
    "The static half of each Day 1 Glue job's DefaultArguments, copied from",
    "infra/modules/day1/glue_jobs.tf. In AWS the Glue service merges a job's",
    "DefaultArguments with the Arguments of a given run, the run winning; the",
    "local bridge (glue_bridge.py) reproduces that merge so a local job sees",
    "the same flags it would in the cloud.",
    "",
    "Only the constant arguments are listed. --p_run_date, --p_batch_id and",
    "--p_region are Terraform variables there and are always supplied by the",
    "state machine here, so a default for them would never be used. The",
    "service-managed arguments (--TempDir, --extra-py-files,",
    "--job-bookmark-option, ...) are omitted too: run-glue.sh provides their",
    "local equivalents (--py-files, the openpyxl install) itself.",
    "",
    "Why this file matters: the state machine passes --catalog_conn, but every",
    "job script reads --p_catalog_conn. Only DefaultArguments closes that gap,",
    "here exactly as in the cloud. {bucket} is replaced with BUCKET_NAME."
  ],
  "jobs": {
